==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The Zory in this stage appear to have buffed stats and are a force to be reckoned with, they do plenty of damage and always spawn in groups of 2. When you fully destroy the 2 original Zories, they will each be replaced twice for a total of 6 Zories in the whole stage.

Since Zory's burrow range is so short (625 only) that usually means he ends up getting past all of your tanks and messing up your Ubers, Dragons or Cyborgs. Keep this in mind when fighting this fast attacking monster and prepare with constantly spawning Rare/Special [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] to help keep them at bay. Special mention to [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Lumbercat]] as his fast attack speed will help deal with Metal Hippoe if you don't bring any critical hitters.

The Heavenly Hippoe and Gabriel can become very obnoxious and end up making life a little difficult for your tanks so anti-Angel units are a plus.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The trick here is to start spawning a cheap and fast meatshield ([[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|C. Wall]] or [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Reg]]/[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|C. Macho]] works well here) as soon as the Metal Hippoe spawns, forcing the Zombie units to burrow as early as possible which gives yourself as much space between the Zombies and your base as possible. Defeat the Zoge and stock up on a Zombie Killer but save as much as you can for when the first Zory spawns.

Once Zory comes out you'll want to keep that meatshield spam up and prepare to spawn your reserve Zombie Killer(s) in response to him burrowing. Try to time it just right.

When Zomboe and Heavenly Hippoe spawn, you'll probably still be dealing with the first Zory but 2 more Zories are going to head your way! This is a perfect chance to practice burrow-stopping with your [[Cat Cannon]] and getting those Zombie Killers in a good position. The Zories are the real struggle of the match so don't be afraid to restart if the timing gets you down.

In the end, the enemies are pretty similar so anti-Zombie Cats, Critter Cats and maybe an anti-Angel cat will help if you still struggle with the Gabriel/H. Hippoe combo.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Metal Hippoes spawn all alone again, joined by a few Zoge by the time he gets close to your base. You can stall for a bit to save up some worker levels. The minor threats start to come out soon and you will need a way to deal with the Gory Dark or he'll wipe your stalling meatshields. Once the Gory and the Gabriels are gone, you'll finish off the Metal Hippoe with either critical hitters or with rapid attackers like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]]. As a plus, Ramen Cat helps to stall the Angel enemies. Save Uber spawns for after the main fight starts.

Once Metal Hippoe is down you'll head to the enemy base and Cadaver Bear & company spawn. While you're being knocked back the Bear is burrowing right through to your Ubers. Take this time to spawn your Ubers so they're ready to fight as soon as C. Bear surfaces. Taking him down quickly is the best way to victory because once Dark Otter and Zigge catch up to him and the Gory bros, the match gets a lot harder.

Fight like normal after you get C. Bear to the surface, making sure to use your long range units to beat C. Bear's 360 range. After that its a smooth walk to the base as only Heavenly Hippoe, Zoge and Zigge continue to spawn at this point.

Bringing Zombie Killers is a must, also anti-Dark and anti-Angel Cats are going to help a lot. If you want to bring critical cats instead of bringing Ramen and Weedwacker Cat, you can bring [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] since they both can serve as meatshields and both have decent crit (the latter requires [[Talents]]). Either way, Metal Hippoe is the least of our worries in this stage.

